# Optional Phone-Tilt Entrance Look-Around

Status: DONE
Milestone: M37 Permission-gated phone orientation controls the room camera
Dependencies: 29_GROUNDED_PAINTED_BAKERY_SCENE.todo; 39_ARCHITECTURAL_BAKERY_FACADE.todo

## Purpose

The owner requests phone gyroscope/orientation input for the same interior
look-around currently driven by a pointer.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve the entry controller and current pending canopy work.
- [x] Add an optional Phone tilt button only for supported secure touch/coarse browsers.
- [x] Request permission only from its tap, never automatically on page load.
- [x] Calibrate the first usable sample, map screen rotation, bound and smooth look input.
- [x] Retain the fixed building, existing room camera and opt-in poster fallback.
- [x] Stop sensor listeners on toggle-off, entry, skip, hidden/pagehide, preferences and links.
- [x] Keep actual controls readable; bypass the optional scene if enlarged controls cannot fit.
- [x] Check pure angle mapping and browser permission/lifecycle fixtures.
- [x] Complete combined canopy/site reviews, refresh artifacts/docs and publish.

## Acceptance criteria

- Phone tilt uses the same bounded look variables, not a separate distorted room.
- No orientation samples are stored or uploaded; no permission request before a tap.
- Denied/rejected/missing/null data leaves a clear inactive state and working entry/Skip.
- No late permission response can start listening after dismissal.
- Screen changes recalibrate rather than jumping; reduced motion remains authoritative.
- Unsupported browsers retain the ordinary entrance and native fallback.
- Synthetic browser evidence is not physical iPhone/Android sensor verification.

